course: dictionary
lesson: 2085
title: Consumer: the buyer and the eater
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A consumer is a person who buys or uses goods and services. Goods are things you can hold, like shoes or bread. Services are things people do for you, like a haircut or a bus ride.
explain: Scientists use consumer in a different way. «Consumers are living things that get their food by eating other living things.» A rabbit eats grass, so the rabbit is a consumer. Grass makes its own food, so it is not one.
explain: Use the clues around the word to find the right meaning. In a shop, look for words about buying. In a food chain, look for words about eating and sunlight. «Every food chain starts with a producer, a plant or alga that makes its own food from sunlight; the animals that eat are consumers.» Here the producer is the plant, and the consumers are the animals that eat it.
fact: A consumer buys or uses goods and services.
fact: In science, a consumer is a living thing that gets its energy by eating other plants or animals.
fact: A primary consumer eats plants, and a secondary consumer eats other animals.
fact: A producer is a plant or alga that makes its own food from sunlight.
fact: Consumer rights include getting safe goods and a refund for things that break.
exercise: In a food chain, «the animals that eat are consumers». Which living thing is a producer? | *A plant or alga that makes its own food | A fox that eats rabbits | A rabbit that eats grass
exercise: A rabbit eats grass. What is the rabbit in a food chain? | Consumer goods | A shop | A producer | *A consumer
exercise: Mia buys a toy that breaks on the first day. Which word names Mia? | *A consumer | A plant | A circuit breaker | A producer
test: A fox eats rabbits. Is the fox a primary consumer or a secondary consumer? | A plant | A producer | *A secondary consumer | A primary consumer
test: Which word names a living thing that makes its own food from sunlight? | *A producer | Consumer goods | A secondary consumer | A consumer
exam: «Consumers are living things that get their food by eating other living things.» Which sentence uses consumer in the same way? | Goods and services cost money | *The owl eats mice, so it is a consumer | The sun gives light to the plants | The shopper bought a new coat, a consumer of goods
